     Dear All
     
     With yet more apologies for my rather over-enthusiastic summarising 
     last time - here is a useful subsequent comment from Peter Stern:
     
     
     Dear Nick:
     
     Since I have now received this message thrice, I feel that a comment 
     is permitted me.  The changes you suggest force every user to set up 
     his profile correctly.  If you make it a default profile, it doesn't 
     take into account the fact that different users may login from 
     different places with different keyboards.  If the user himself uses 
     different "keyboards" at different times, the profile has to reflect 
     this.
     
     A simpler approach seems to simply put the line:
     -pn -xkbmap digital_uk_pcxal
     into the file:  /usr/lib/X11/Xserver.conf
     This then solves the problem for everybody painlessly.
     Read the file: /usr/lib/X11/xkb/keymaps.dir for more details.
     
     Regards,
     Peter Stern
     
     
     Thanks again
     
     Nick

