To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: lockfile not found?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078705511394

As usual, lightning fast responses!
Thanks John and Bob


Original Post:
> Any ideas what the sirihs00.lock not found refers to in the msg below?
>
> # cd /var/spool/mail
> # ls *.lock
> sirihs00.lock not found
> dimauroc.lock  wilsoj93.lock
> # ls sirihs00.lock

John Speno responded
I think it means that the file was there for a short time, but not long
enought for ls to do a 'stat' on it.

In other words, it's nothing bad. You just missed it.

Bob Sloane responded
> # ls *.lock

When you typed in the command the shell expanded the *.lock, and the
file sirihs00.lock existed. By the time ls got around to listing the
file, it had been deleted, causing the "not found" message.

