Subject: SUMMARY: AdvFS BMT parameters
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96078705511354

Thanks to Girish Phadke, who explained how to use showfile(8) to
reveal a domain's BMT increment size.

First cd to the .tags directory under an existing fileset in the
domain, eg,

# cd /usr/.tags

then

# showfile -x M-6

The output will resemble the following, 

           Id  Vol  PgSz  Pages  XtntType  Segs  SegSz  Log  Perf  File
  fffffffa.0000    1    16   2050    simple    **     **  ftx  100%  M-6

      extentMap: 1
          pageOff    pageCnt     vol    volBlock    blockCnt
                0          2       1          32          32
                2        128       1        8816        2048
              130        128       1      130128        2048
              258        128       1      347856        2048
               :          :        :         :            :

The second and subsequent 'pageCnt' values equal the BMT increment (or
'-x' parameter) with which the domain was created - in this case, the
default value of 128.  I then used this value to voladd additional
space to my usr domain (see original post below).

Thanks again Girish!  Cheers,
