In response to my question, several people referred me to different
vendors who sell them. The most interesting response I received was from
Paul Kitwin who suggested the following: 

On Wed, 1 Apr 1998, Paul Kitwin wrote:
> DON'T BUY THEM!!!!!!!!!!!
> 
> We have a TL894 (4 TZ89s w/ the robot arm thing).  I priced the labels,
> and they where expensive.  As I recall they were about a buck a label.
> You have to buy them from ATL directly.
> 
> Anyway, I use a type 39 Barcode font, set an MS Excel spreadsheet to
> 57.75 points across and 25 points high.  Set the font size to 36 run it
> through an HP Laser Jet and boom.  For about 2 cents per label, I have
> my own, custom labels.  Since our library runs the backups for 5
> machines, I have a different color label for each machine.  Makes thing
> easy to read.

